  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A small block slides down from the top of hemisphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;at which the block will lose contact with the surface of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. (Assume there is no friction between the block and the hemisphere)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/db2a7d0a-d7c8-4316-9448-a72b334da3ca-image.png\" style=\"width: 367px; height: 183px;\" /></p>",
